<article class="env-remark" id="4BF4D1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/4BF4D1">Remark <span data-tag="4BF4D1">5.2.8.7</span>.</a> Suppose given a pair of adjoint functors $\xymatrix {\calC  \ar @< .4ex>[r]^{F} &amp;  \calD . \ar @< .4ex>[l]^{G}}$ Let $f$ be a morphism in $\calC $ and $g$ a morphism in $\calD $. Then $f \perp G(g)$ if and only if $F(f) \perp g$. </p>
